# Package metadata; the preferred-citation DOI belongs to the paper preprint.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: When using this viewer, cite the associated IEEE IECON 2026 OPF paper [25] (preferred citation below)
  and identify supplementary package version 1.0.1. Also cite [26] when discussing LUT reduction. The
  paper DOI is not a DOI for this package.
type: software
title: Interactive supplementary material for the IEEE IECON 2026 open-phase-fault paper
authors:
- family-names: Yepes
  given-names: Alejandro G.
version: 1.0.1
date-released: '2026-10-07'
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: Self-contained interactive viewer associated with the IEEE IECON 2026 OPF paper [25], using its compact-LUT
  implementation and the supporting reduction approach of [26]. Explores sampled steady-state current
  references, required voltages, torque, and copper losses. The adjusted NSBE-FRML mean-torque comparison
  differs from the original paper comparison.
keywords:
- open-phase fault
- six-phase PMSM
- current references
- torque-speed range
- compact lookup tables
- IEEE IECON 2026
